here. He opened his eyes, the blue light of the console now seeming to pulse in time with his erratic heartbeat. The code on the screen was no longer static; it was shifting, rearranging itself in ways that defied logic. He leaned forward, his breath catching in his throat. Something was wrong. Deeply, fundamentally wrong. And it was getting closer."
